  "notes": {
    "continentalBoundaries": "Europe/Asia: Urals, Ural River, Caspian Sea, Greater Caucasus watershed, Black Sea and Turkish straits. Africa/Asia: Suez. North/South America: Panama/Colombia boundary. Asia/Oceania: New Guinea belongs to Oceania; the rest of Indonesia is grouped with Asia.",
    "islands": "Caribbean islands and Clipperton are grouped with North America; Madeira, the Azores and the Canary Islands with Europe, as Portugal and Spain are in UN M49, GeoNames and the CIA World Factbook, and no source assigns these islands to Africa (the owner, 2026-11-05: follow the sources); Polynesia/Micronesia/Melanesia with Oceania. Otherwise, island location is not inherited from the administering state. Mediterranean island assignments retain the explicit existing European/Asian convention rather than automatically following tectonic plates.",
    "scope": "FRA includes Clipperton (EU+NA); PRT includes Madeira and the Azores (EU). Separately coded French territories retain their own memberships. COL includes San Andrés/Providencia and VEN includes Isla de Aves (SA+NA). The 39 extra Maps regional questions are omitted as exercises, not erased from whole-place metadata. Pro map questions reuse approved Maps core/overview pictures; continent metadata describes the named place, not only the rendered crop.",
    "transcontinental": "Russia, Turkey, Kazakhstan, Georgia and Azerbaijan cross the documented Europe/Asia divide. Egypt includes Sinai; Indonesia includes western New Guinea; USA includes Hawaii; Chile includes Rapa Nui; Spain includes Ceuta, Melilla and the plazas de soberanía on the North African coast.",
    "subantarcticReview": "The owner approved the named Antarctic-island discovery convention on 2 November 2026; on 5 November the owner moved Amsterdam and Saint Paul to Africa, as UN M49 has ATF, replacing that call for those two islands, as in Maps. The decision and UN M49 comparison remain under taxonomyReview. ATF’s Scattered Islands remain African. No continent is inferred from Antarctic-program management.",
    "region": "The separate Region field retains the named place’s primary regional vocabulary; it does not claim to enumerate all remote-island subregions."
  },
  "references": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.nationalgeographic.org/national-geographic-map-policy",
      "use": "Europe/Asia boundary; our search retains both memberships rather than the source single-country classification."
